    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d118">

                <pb facs="0125" n="119" sameAs="frus:frus1894app1/pg119"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Gresham to Mr. Bayard.</hi></head>
                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Telegram.]</seg></opener>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Department of State</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1893-10-03"><hi rendition="#italic">October 3,
                        1893</hi></date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p>Yours of September 20 received. Lord Rosebery’s suggestion has been carefully
                    considered, and the President still prefers that all negotiations for concurrent
                    action by the two Governments necessary to <pb facs="0126" n="120"
                        xml:id="pg120"/> make the award and recommendations of the Bering Sea
                    Tribunal effective be conducted by you at London, and my instructions cabled
                    September 16 are repeated.</p>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
